*Combinatorics of Indistinguishable Particles:* For a single-particle basis ${bar.v 1 chevron.r, dots, bar.v N chevron.r}$, two-particle states for identical bosons must be symmetric under particle exchange (spanned by states of the form $bar.v i chevron.r bar.v j chevron.r + bar.v j chevron.r bar.v i chevron.r$). Identical fermions must be antisymmetric (spanned by states of the form $bar.v i chevron.r bar.v j chevron.r - bar.v j chevron.r bar.v i chevron.r$ with $i != j$).
